*> Implementation test of the entity metadata entry codecs of proto/src/entity-metadata.cob: one entry
*> of the 00 §13.1 list for each of the 44 serializers of 00 §13.2 and 46 §12 (PB-METADATA-ENTRY-X of
*> PROTO.cpy), and the 0xFF terminator. A writer that cannot encode an entry appends nothing and
*> sets PB-ERROR; a failed read leaves PB-POS where it was and yields an all-zero entry. Expected
*> bytes are written out by hand from the field tables of the documents; the entry is shown by the
*> test helper TEST-DUMP-METADATA.
 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
 PROGRAM-ID. TEST-ENTITY-METADATA.
 DATA DIVISION.
 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
 COPY PROTO.
 COPY TESTLIB.
 01 WS-CAPACITY            BINARY-LONG VALUE 64.
 01 WS-NAME                PIC X(100).
 01 WS-WANT-HEX            PIC X(1024).
 01 WS-WANT-DUMP           PIC X(1100).
 01 WS-DUMP                PIC X(1100).
 01 WS-EDIT                PIC -(9)9.
 01 WS-PTR                 BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-I                   BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-BIG                 PIC X(1100).
 01 WS-EDIT2               PIC -(9)9.
 01 WS-COUNT               BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-VALUE               BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-HIGH                BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-LOW                 BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-HEX2                PIC XX.
 01 WS-DIGITS              PIC X(16) VALUE "0123456789abcdef".
 01 WS-A                   PIC X VALUE "a".
 01 WS-END                 PIC X VALUE LOW-VALUE.
 01 WS-ONE                 BINARY-LONG VALUE 1.
 PROCEDURE DIVISION.
     CALL "PB-INIT" USING PB-BUFFER WS-CAPACITY
     PERFORM SERIALIZER-CASES
     PERFORM VERBATIM-CASES
     PERFORM PUT-ERRORS
     PERFORM GET-ERRORS
     CALL "PB-FREE" USING PB-BUFFER
     STOP RUN.

