     MOVE FUNCTION HEX-TO-CHAR("00") TO PB-MX-DATA(1:1)
     MOVE 1 TO PB-MX-DATA-LENGTH
     MOVE "COMPONENT End root" TO WS-NAME
     PERFORM PUT-FAILS
     PERFORM NEW-ENTRY
     MOVE 5 TO PB-MX-SERIALIZER
     MOVE FUNCTION HEX-TO-CHAR("63") TO PB-MX-DATA(1:1)
     MOVE 1 TO PB-MX-DATA-LENGTH
     MOVE "COMPONENT unknown root type" TO WS-NAME
     PERFORM PUT-FAILS
     PERFORM NEW-ENTRY
     MOVE 5 TO PB-MX-SERIALIZER
     MOVE -1 TO PB-MX-DATA-LENGTH
     MOVE "COMPONENT data length -1" TO WS-NAME
     PERFORM PUT-FAILS
     PERFORM NEW-ENTRY
     MOVE 5 TO PB-MX-SERIALIZER
     MOVE 513 TO PB-MX-DATA-LENGTH
     MOVE "COMPONENT data length 513" TO WS-NAME
     PERFORM PUT-FAILS
     PERFORM NEW-ENTRY
     MOVE 16 TO PB-MX-SERIALIZER
     MOVE FUNCTION HEX-TO-CHAR("c801") TO PB-MX-DATA(1:2)
     MOVE 2 TO PB-MX-DATA-LENGTH
     MOVE "PARTICLE type 200" TO WS-NAME
     PERFORM PUT-FAILS
     PERFORM NEW-ENTRY
     MOVE 17 TO PB-MX-SERIALIZER
     MOVE FUNCTION HEX-TO-CHAR("0137ff") TO PB-MX-DATA(1:3)
     MOVE 3 TO PB-MX-DATA-LENGTH
     MOVE "PARTICLES with a trailing byte" TO WS-NAME
     PERFORM PUT-FAILS
     PERFORM NEW-ENTRY
     MOVE 17 TO PB-MX-SERIALIZER
     MOVE FUNCTION HEX-TO-CHAR("ffffffff0f") TO PB-MX-DATA(1:5)
     MOVE 5 TO PB-MX-DATA-LENGTH
     MOVE "PARTICLES count -1" TO WS-NAME
     PERFORM PUT-FAILS
     PERFORM NEW-ENTRY
     MOVE 17 TO PB-MX-SERIALIZER
     MOVE FUNCTION HEX-TO-CHAR("0237") TO PB-MX-DATA(1:2)
     MOVE 2 TO PB-MX-DATA-LENGTH
     MOVE "PARTICLES count 2 with one particle" TO WS-NAME
     PERFORM PUT-FAILS
     PERFORM NEW-ENTRY
     MOVE 34 TO PB-MX-SERIALIZER
     MOVE FUNCTION HEX-TO-CHAR("00") TO PB-MX-DATA(1:1)
     MOVE 1 TO PB-MX-DATA-LENGTH
     MOVE "PAINTING_VARIANT inline form" TO WS-NAME
     PERFORM PUT-FAILS
     PERFORM NEW-ENTRY
     MOVE 33 TO PB-MX-SERIALIZER
     MOVE 1 TO PB-MX-PRESENT
     MOVE FUNCTION HEX-TO-CHAR("0141") TO PB-MX-DATA(1:2)
     MOVE 2 TO PB-MX-DATA-LENGTH
     MOVE "OPTIONAL_GLOBAL_POS with an invalid identifier" TO WS-NAME
     PERFORM PUT-FAILS
     PERFORM NEW-ENTRY
     MOVE 33 TO PB-MX-SERIALIZER
     MOVE 1 TO PB-MX-PRESENT
     MOVE FUNCTION HEX-TO-CHAR("013a00000000") TO PB-MX-DATA(1:6)
     MOVE 6 TO PB-MX-DATA-LENGTH
     MOVE "OPTIONAL_GLOBAL_POS cut short" TO WS-NAME
     PERFORM PUT-FAILS
     PERFORM NEW-ENTRY
     MOVE 41 TO PB-MX-SERIALIZER
     MOVE FUNCTION HEX-TO-CHAR("000000000000") TO PB-MX-DATA(1:6)
     MOVE 6 TO PB-MX-DATA-LENGTH
     MOVE "RESOLVABLE_PROFILE partial with half a skin patch" TO WS-NAME
     PERFORM PUT-FAILS
     PERFORM NEW-ENTRY
     MOVE 41 TO PB-MX-SERIALIZER
     MOVE FUNCTION HEX-TO-CHAR("00000011") TO PB-MX-DATA(1:4)
     MOVE 4 TO PB-MX-DATA-LENGTH
     MOVE "RESOLVABLE_PROFILE with 17 properties" TO WS-NAME
     PERFORM PUT-FAILS
     PERFORM NEW-ENTRY
     MOVE 41 TO PB-MX-SERIALIZER
     MOVE FUNCTION HEX-TO-CHAR("000131") TO PB-MX-DATA(1:3)
     MOVE 3 TO PB-MX-DATA-LENGTH
     MOVE "RESOLVABLE_PROFILE name of 49 bytes" TO WS-NAME
     PERFORM PUT-FAILS
     PERFORM NEW-ENTRY
     MOVE 41 TO PB-MX-SERIALIZER
     MOVE FUNCTION HEX-TO-CHAR("0001ffffffff0f") TO PB-MX-DATA(1:7)
     MOVE 7 TO PB-MX-DATA-LENGTH
     MOVE "RESOLVABLE_PROFILE name length -1" TO WS-NAME
     PERFORM PUT-FAILS
*>   a failing entry leaves the bytes of an earlier one alone
     CALL "PB-RESET" USING PB-BUFFER
     PERFORM NEW-ENTRY
     MOVE 8 TO PB-MX-INDEX PB-MX-SERIALIZER
     MOVE 1 TO PB-MX-INT
     CALL "PB-PUT-METADATA-ENTRY-X" USING PB-BUFFER PB-METADATA-ENTRY-X
     MOVE 5 TO PB-MX-SERIALIZER
     MOVE 3 TO PB-MX-DATA-LENGTH
     CALL "PB-PUT-METADATA-ENTRY-X" USING PB-BUFFER PB-METADATA-ENTRY-X
     MOVE "test entity-metadata a failed put keeps the earlier bytes" TO TL-CASE
     CALL "TEST-BUFFER-HEX" USING PB-BUFFER TL-OBSERVED
     MOVE SPACES TO WS-DUMP
     STRING "E" PB-ERROR " " FUNCTION TRIM(TL-OBSERVED) DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO WS-DUMP
     MOVE "T" TO TL-MODE
     MOVE "E1 080801" TO TL-EXPECTED
     MOVE SPACES TO TL-OBSERVED
     MOVE WS-DUMP TO TL-OBSERVED
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT.

 GET-ERRORS.
     MOVE SPACES TO WS-WANT-HEX
     MOVE "empty buffer" TO WS-NAME
     PERFORM GET-FAILS
     MOVE "00" TO WS-WANT-HEX
     MOVE "index without serializer" TO WS-NAME
     PERFORM GET-FAILS
     MOVE "002c" TO WS-WANT-HEX
     MOVE "serializer 44" TO WS-NAME
     PERFORM GET-FAILS
     MOVE "0080" TO WS-WANT-HEX
     MOVE "serializer VarInt cut short" TO WS-NAME
     PERFORM GET-FAILS
     MOVE "0000" TO WS-WANT-HEX
     MOVE "BYTE without value" TO WS-NAME
     PERFORM GET-FAILS
     MOVE "0808" TO WS-WANT-HEX
     MOVE "BOOLEAN without value" TO WS-NAME
     PERFORM GET-FAILS
     MOVE "03033f" TO WS-WANT-HEX
     MOVE "FLOAT cut short" TO WS-NAME
     PERFORM GET-FAILS
     MOVE "0202ff" TO WS-WANT-HEX
     MOVE "LONG cut short" TO WS-NAME
     PERFORM GET-FAILS
     MOVE "0404056162" TO WS-WANT-HEX
     MOVE "STRING cut short" TO WS-NAME
     PERFORM GET-FAILS
     MOVE "0404ac02" TO WS-WANT-HEX
     MOVE "STRING of 300 bytes does not fit the record" TO WS-NAME
     MOVE 300 TO WS-COUNT
     PERFORM GET-FAILS-LONG
     MOVE "0404ffffffff0f" TO WS-WANT-HEX
     MOVE "STRING length -1" TO WS-NAME
     PERFORM GET-FAILS
     MOVE "0c0cffffffff0f" TO WS-WANT-HEX
     MOVE "DIRECTION -1" TO WS-NAME
     PERFORM GET-FAILS
     MOVE "1212ffffffff0f0903" TO WS-WANT-HEX
     MOVE "VILLAGER_DATA type -1" TO WS-NAME
     PERFORM GET-FAILS
     MOVE "121202ffffffff0f03" TO WS-WANT-HEX
     MOVE "VILLAGER_DATA profession -1" TO WS-NAME
     PERFORM GET-FAILS
     MOVE "12120209ffffffff0f" TO WS-WANT-HEX
     MOVE "VILLAGER_DATA level -1" TO WS-NAME
     PERFORM GET-FAILS
     MOVE "07070103" TO WS-WANT-HEX
     MOVE "0100" TO WS-WANT-HEX(9:)
     MOVE "ITEM_STACK with a component patch" TO WS-NAME
     PERFORM GET-FAILS
     MOVE "0b0b01000001" TO WS-WANT-HEX
     MOVE "OPTIONAL_BLOCK_POS cut short" TO WS-NAME
     PERFORM GET-FAILS
     MOVE "0d0d0100" TO WS-WANT-HEX
     MOVE "OPTIONAL_LIVING_ENTITY_REFERENCE cut short" TO WS-NAME
     PERFORM GET-FAILS
     MOVE "0505" TO WS-WANT-HEX
     MOVE "COMPONENT without value" TO WS-NAME
     PERFORM GET-FAILS
     MOVE "050563" TO WS-WANT-HEX
     MOVE "COMPONENT unknown root type" TO WS-NAME
     PERFORM GET-FAILS
     MOVE "050500" TO WS-WANT-HEX
     MOVE "COMPONENT End root" TO WS-NAME
     PERFORM GET-FAILS
     MOVE "0606010800" TO WS-WANT-HEX
     MOVE "OPTIONAL_COMPONENT cut short" TO WS-NAME
     PERFORM GET-FAILS
     MOVE "10101500ff" TO WS-WANT-HEX
     MOVE "PARTICLE cut short" TO WS-NAME
     PERFORM GET-FAILS
     MOVE "1111ffffffff0f" TO WS-WANT-HEX
     MOVE "PARTICLES count -1" TO WS-NAME
     PERFORM GET-FAILS
     MOVE "11110237" TO WS-WANT-HEX
     MOVE "PARTICLES count 2 with one particle" TO WS-NAME
     PERFORM GET-FAILS
     MOVE "222200" TO WS-WANT-HEX
     MOVE "PAINTING_VARIANT inline form" TO WS-NAME
     PERFORM GET-FAILS
     MOVE "212101" TO WS-WANT-HEX
     MOVE "OPTIONAL_GLOBAL_POS cut short" TO WS-NAME
     PERFORM GET-FAILS
     MOVE "29290001" TO WS-WANT-HEX
     MOVE "RESOLVABLE_PROFILE cut short" TO WS-NAME
     PERFORM GET-FAILS
     MOVE "2929000105" TO WS-WANT-HEX
     MOVE "RESOLVABLE_PROFILE name cut short" TO WS-NAME
     PERFORM GET-FAILS
     MOVE "2929000131" TO WS-WANT-HEX
     MOVE "RESOLVABLE_PROFILE name of 49 bytes" TO WS-NAME
     PERFORM GET-FAILS
     MOVE "29290100" TO WS-WANT-HEX
     MOVE "RESOLVABLE_PROFILE full form cut short" TO WS-NAME
     PERFORM GET-FAILS
     MOVE "292900000011" TO WS-WANT-HEX
     MOVE "RESOLVABLE_PROFILE with 17 properties" TO WS-NAME
     PERFORM GET-FAILS
     MOVE "292900000001" TO WS-WANT-HEX
     MOVE "RESOLVABLE_PROFILE property cut short" TO WS-NAME
     PERFORM GET-FAILS
     MOVE "2929000000" TO WS-WANT-HEX
     MOVE "01c101" TO WS-WANT-HEX(11:)
     MOVE "RESOLVABLE_PROFILE property name of 193 bytes" TO WS-NAME
     PERFORM GET-FAILS
     MOVE "2929" & "00000000000000" TO WS-WANT-HEX
     MOVE "RESOLVABLE_PROFILE skin patch cut short" TO WS-NAME
     PERFORM GET-FAILS
*>   a 513-byte component does not fit PB-MX-DATA: 8 bytes, a 2-byte length, 502 characters, End
     MOVE "0505" & "0a08000474657874" & "01f6" TO WS-WANT-HEX
     MOVE "COMPONENT of 513 bytes does not fit the record" TO WS-NAME
     MOVE 502 TO WS-COUNT
     PERFORM GET-FAILS-LONG.

 NEW-ENTRY.
     INITIALIZE PB-METADATA-ENTRY-X.

*> Puts the record, compares the bytes with WS-WANT-HEX, reads them back and compares the shown
*> entry with WS-WANT-DUMP followed by " ok".
 ROUND-TRIP.
     CALL "PB-RESET" USING PB-BUFFER
     CALL "PB-PUT-METADATA-ENTRY-X" USING PB-BUFFER PB-METADATA-ENTRY-X
     MOVE SPACES TO TL-CASE
     STRING "test entity-metadata put of " FUNCTION TRIM(WS-NAME) DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO TL-CASE
     CALL "TEST-BUFFER-HEX" USING PB-BUFFER TL-OBSERVED
     IF PB-ERROR NOT = 0
         MOVE "ERROR" TO TL-OBSERVED
     END-IF
     MOVE WS-WANT-HEX TO TL-EXPECTED
     MOVE "T" TO TL-MODE
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     CALL "TEST-FILL-HEX" USING WS-WANT-HEX PB-BUFFER
     CALL "PB-GET-METADATA-ENTRY-X" USING PB-BUFFER PB-METADATA-ENTRY-X
     CALL "TEST-DUMP-METADATA" USING PB-METADATA-ENTRY-X WS-DUMP
     MOVE SPACES TO TL-CASE
     STRING "test entity-metadata get of " FUNCTION TRIM(WS-NAME) DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO TL-CASE
     PERFORM SHOW-RESULT
     MOVE SPACES TO WS-WANT-HEX WS-WANT-DUMP.

*> TL-OBSERVED := WS-DUMP and the read outcome; TL-EXPECTED := WS-WANT-DUMP and " ok"; asserts.
 SHOW-RESULT.
     MOVE SPACES TO TL-OBSERVED TL-EXPECTED
     MOVE 1 TO WS-PTR
     STRING FUNCTION TRIM(WS-DUMP) DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO TL-OBSERVED WITH POINTER WS-PTR
     IF PB-ERROR = 0 AND PB-POS = PB-LENGTH
         STRING " ok" DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO TL-OBSERVED WITH POINTER WS-PTR
     ELSE
         MOVE PB-ERROR TO WS-EDIT
         STRING " e" FUNCTION TRIM(WS-EDIT) DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO TL-OBSERVED WITH POINTER WS-PTR
         MOVE PB-POS TO WS-EDIT
         STRING " p" FUNCTION TRIM(WS-EDIT) DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO TL-OBSERVED WITH POINTER WS-PTR
     END-IF
     MOVE 1 TO WS-PTR
     STRING FUNCTION TRIM(WS-WANT-DUMP) " ok" DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO TL-EXPECTED
         WITH POINTER WS-PTR
     MOVE "T" TO TL-MODE
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT.

*> The put of the record must set PB-ERROR and append nothing.
 PUT-FAILS.
     CALL "PB-RESET" USING PB-BUFFER
     CALL "PB-PUT-METADATA-ENTRY-X" USING PB-BUFFER PB-METADATA-ENTRY-X
     MOVE SPACES TO TL-CASE
     STRING "test entity-metadata put of " FUNCTION TRIM(WS-NAME)
         " sets PB-ERROR and appends nothing" DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO TL-CASE
     MOVE SPACES TO TL-OBSERVED
     MOVE PB-ERROR TO WS-EDIT
     MOVE PB-LENGTH TO WS-EDIT2
     STRING "error " FUNCTION TRIM(WS-EDIT) " length " FUNCTION TRIM(WS-EDIT2)
         DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO TL-OBSERVED
     MOVE "T" TO TL-MODE
     MOVE "error 1 length 0" TO TL-EXPECTED
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT.

*> Reads WS-WANT-HEX: PB-ERROR set, PB-POS 0 and an all-zero entry.
 GET-FAILS.
     CALL "TEST-FILL-HEX" USING WS-WANT-HEX PB-BUFFER
     PERFORM GET-CHECK.

*> The same with WS-COUNT more "a" bytes after the hex, then an End byte.
 GET-FAILS-LONG.
     CALL "TEST-FILL-HEX" USING WS-WANT-HEX PB-BUFFER
     PERFORM WS-COUNT TIMES
         CALL "PB-APPEND-BYTES" USING PB-BUFFER WS-A WS-ONE
     END-PERFORM
     CALL "PB-APPEND-BYTES" USING PB-BUFFER WS-END WS-ONE
     PERFORM GET-CHECK.

 GET-CHECK.
     MOVE 77 TO PB-MX-INDEX
     MOVE 77 TO PB-MX-INT
     CALL "PB-GET-METADATA-ENTRY-X" USING PB-BUFFER PB-METADATA-ENTRY-X
     CALL "TEST-DUMP-METADATA" USING PB-METADATA-ENTRY-X WS-DUMP
     MOVE SPACES TO TL-CASE
     STRING "test entity-metadata get of " FUNCTION TRIM(WS-NAME)
         " fails, PB-POS stays and the entry is zero" DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO TL-CASE
     MOVE SPACES TO TL-OBSERVED TL-EXPECTED
     MOVE 1 TO WS-PTR
     STRING FUNCTION TRIM(WS-DUMP) DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO TL-OBSERVED WITH POINTER WS-PTR
     MOVE PB-ERROR TO WS-EDIT
     STRING " e" FUNCTION TRIM(WS-EDIT) DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO TL-OBSERVED WITH POINTER WS-PTR
     MOVE PB-POS TO WS-EDIT
     STRING " p" FUNCTION TRIM(WS-EDIT) DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO TL-OBSERVED WITH POINTER WS-PTR
     MOVE "0.0=0 e1 p0" TO TL-EXPECTED
     MOVE "T" TO TL-MODE
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE SPACES TO WS-WANT-HEX.

*> WS-HEX2 := the two lowercase hex digits of WS-VALUE (0 to 255).
 HEX-BYTE.
     DIVIDE WS-VALUE BY 16 GIVING WS-HIGH REMAINDER WS-LOW
     ADD 1 TO WS-HIGH WS-LOW
     MOVE WS-DIGITS(WS-HIGH:1) TO WS-HEX2(1:1)
     MOVE WS-DIGITS(WS-LOW:1) TO WS-HEX2(2:1).
 END PROGRAM TEST-ENTITY-METADATA.
 COPY PROTOTEST.
